   "titulo": "How it forms",
   "texto": [
    "**abbia / sia** (present congiuntive of the average or essere) + participle: **abbia capito** (you understand), **sia venuto** (you have come).",
    "With **essere**, the participle agrees: **sia venuta** (have come, she)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Common expressions",
   "texto": [
    "With a doubt, desire or valuation is usually preferred the congiuntive: **Non credo che sia venuto**, **È possibile che abbia capito**. With some verbs, including **credere**, the sign may also appear when the content is presented as a certainty or in certain records.",
    "Learn the common pattern and care for meaning and registration."
   ]
